msgid "This is a human readable name for the :ref:`unit` with the :ref:`positioning`. The field can be manually entered or automatically populated by the system. Best practice for this field is to use the :ref:`name:annotation <unit-name-annotation>` for the :ref:`unit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:365
msgid "positioning:types:assertion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:370
msgid "The type of location of a unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:375
msgid "String selected from controlled list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:390
msgid "``site``, ``aoo``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:395
msgid "This field defines the relationship between a unit and a :ref:`location`. The Staff Researcher must choose one of the two options below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:397
msgid "``site``: the :ref:`location` describes a \"site\" at which the unit is based."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:398
msgid "``aoo``: the :ref:`location` describes a place (usually an administrative area), where the unit is known to have conducted operations or has territorial jurisdiction. When the ``aoo`` is a specific point, such as an intersection or a town (villages, towns and other populated places are usually represented as a point in most gazetteers), then the smallest/lowest level encompassing administrative area should also be entered as a separate claim using the same citation. This is done to capture that when a :ref:`unit` is reported to have conducted an operation in a specific place (represented by a point or small polygon), such an operation, by its very nature, means operating in the area around the \"point\" of the town or village."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:400
msgid "The specifics of this \"smallest/lowest level encompassing administrative area\" vary from country to country. Generally, the following should be used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:402
msgid ":ref:`location:admin_level:qa` of ``3`` or ``4`` if :ref:`location` is drawn from UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA). This means the :ref:`origin:location` would be ``ocha``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:403
msgid ":ref:`location:admin_level:qa` of ``6`` or lower if :ref:`location` is drawn from OpenStreetMap (OSM). This means the :ref:`origin:location` would be ``osm``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:408
msgid "positioning:base_names:assertion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:413
msgid "A base is a distinctively named building or complex - like a barracks or camp - where the unit is located."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:418 ../../source/units-positionings.rst:737 ../../source/units-positionings.rst:771 ../../source/units-positionings.rst:806
msgid "String"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:433
msgid "``Leopard Base``,  ``Bonny Camp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:438
msgid "The :ref:`positioning:base_names:assertion` attribute adds unit-specific context about a Location. This field is used to record data about units that are located in a distinctively-named building or complex which is not found in the gazetteer, or otherwise cannot be represented as a geographic datapoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:443
msgid "The ``3 Battalion`` in Nigeria is cited as being based in the ``Lubanga Barracks`` in ``Enugu, Enugu State, Nigeria``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:445
msgid "This field should not be used for anything that matches the name or alias of a unit. For example, ``North Sector Police Station`` should not be put in this field if the name of the unit is ``North Sector Police Station``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:449
msgid "positioning:location:refs:assertion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:454
msgid "Unique 32 character identifier of a Location where the unit has a \"site\" or \"area of operations\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:459
msgid "String in UUID format for the :ref:`location` selected from :ref:`id:entity` in the locations sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/units-positionings.rst:474
msgid "``93dcc4a8-8335-4a21-8372-a151c4972c54`` (which is the raw ID for ``Ikorodu (osm, point) 93dcc4a8-8335-4a21-8372-a151c4972c54``)"
